# Nothing in this file is required. The site builds and runs with no .env at all.
#
# It documents the shape of the future integration only. `@nuxtjs/supabase` was
# removed (README § Supabase) precisely because it forced these variables to
# exist before any feature used them.

# Supabase — uncomment together with the first authenticated feature.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_KEY=

# Server-only. Never expose to the client. For Nitro routes that need to bypass
# RLS (e.g. Stripe webhook -> subscription state). If this is ever added, the
# route that reads it must authenticate the caller first — a service-role key
# behind an unauthenticated route is an open database.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=

# Stripe — not yet wired. Documented here so the shape of the future
# integration is obvious. See README § Adding accounts and payments.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
